WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.412
The guide names the automated check for
Gate 2, built in the workbook's Chapter 08.

2
00:00:05.412 --> 00:00:06.250
Why now?

3
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:11.239
The implementation example planned a
read-only check of the two provisioning

4
00:00:11.239 --> 00:00:15.691
mappings for Pass 2, and both
configurations export as JSON through

5
00:00:15.691 --> 00:00:19.375
documented reads, so the check
runs on files, offline, today.

6
00:00:19.375 --> 00:00:21.063
It reads two exports.

7
00:00:21.063 --> 00:00:25.825
The first is the inbound job's
synchronization schema, from Microsoft Graph.

8
00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:31.110
It takes the rules that target the Entra
directory, the enabled mappings to User,

9
00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:35.354
and each attribute's flow type:
Always updates it on every change,

10
00:00:35.354 --> 00:00:38.237
and Object Add Only sets
it only at creation.

11
00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:41.724
The second is the SailPoint
source's provisioning policies.

12
00:00:41.724 --> 00:00:44.583
An Update policy is used
for attribute sync,

13
00:00:44.583 --> 00:00:49.490
a Create policy when the account is
made, and other usage types are ignored.
